// PSS v3.0 LRM — Example 138: Distribution directive weight specification forms (page 209)
struct S {
  rand bit[32] x;
  constraint dist x in [100..102 := 1, 200 := 2, 300 := 5];
}
struct S {
  rand bit[32] x;
  constraint dist (x+6) in [100..102 := 1, 200 := 2, 300 := 5];
}
struct S {
  rand bit[32] x;
  constraint dist x in [100..102 :/ 1, 200 := 2, 300 := 5];
}

In the example above, x is weighted to have a value range [100..102, 200, 300]. Additionally, value
selection is weighted 1/3, 1/3, 1/3, 2, 5.
